# Slice 295 (VAR-OWN-NESTED-AND-REFERENCE; the book :133, :387): both branches of an `if` declare `z`, with different types:
# one place `z` in the activation.  The refusal at the second declaration is the current limit of the implementation, not
# the norm (REPEATED-DECL-TYPED-RECEPTION: the place is to receive the candidate `char: 6`).  On 294: two cells, it ran.
fn: m (int: c) int
    int: r 0
    if: c = 1
        int: z 5
        r: z
    else:
        char: z 6
        r: 2
    ---
    return: r
end: m
int: code 7
int: v m(1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
